      "side": 1,
      "message": "the logic seems ok, but still a question:\n\nwhat if, say, __hw_clock_source_read() \u003d\u003d last_time_deassert_ + min_duration_int_ap_ already, but timer_int_ap_irq_handler() hasn\u0027t been called yet because the tick just happened and we are still sitting in SPI/I2C handler atm.\n\nthen the current int_ap_sts_ is DEASSERTED. and, by calling timer_int_ap_irq_handler() we will: assert \u0027ready\u0027, set int_ap_sts_ \u003d ASSERTED and schedule the timer to fire min_duration_int_ap_ from now.\n\nis it still possible for timer_int_ap_irq_handler() to be fired right after that based on the currently pending TIMER1 interrupt? I hope no, since the first thing timer_int_ap_irq_handler() called here does is clearing the interrupt. but, if yes, the pending handler would immediately deassert \u0027ready\u0027 again, which is not what we want.",
